    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.03), our two strongest plays. **Christian Yelich** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Michael McGreevy, where dynamic platoon advantages and a leadoff spot boost his utility. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** carries a premium projection despite the SP_xERA of 2.85; his 16% park factor uplift and elite stolen base profile make him a must-start, as we prioritize his speed to bolster our scarcest category. **Dillon Dingler** (63.90) and **Josh Smith** (62.54) also stand out as high-floor starters, with both benefiting from strong dynamic platoon edges that project to mitigate the risks posed by their respective opposing starters.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Chase Meidroth** (47.49), who nearly cracked the lineup but ultimately fell short due to the superior daily efficiency scores provided by the middle-infield and outfield logjam. While **Chase Meidroth** offers reliable production, the optimizer favored **Junior Caminero** (61.45) in the UTIL slot, even against a formidable arm like Gerrit Cole, due to **Junior Caminero**\u2019s superior xwOBA and high-leverage order placement. We also continue to monitor the status of **Yordan Alvarez** (57.36); while his xwOBA remains elite at 0.475, his platoon disadvantage today necessitates close monitoring of the official lineup. Managers should note that with most of our roster currently labeled \"Lineup Pending,\" the scores for **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** rely on assumed positioning, and any shifts in the batting order could necessitate a re-evaluation of our daily floor.",
